 inter\n•\n•       Telecom Phones (MLD\, MLW\, SLD\, SLW\, SLP)\n\n\n\n•    
    Applications (Application installed and Icons)\n\n•       Data Jack #s\n
 •       IP Address\n•       Vlans\n\n•       -Kronos Time Clocks\n•       -
 Refrigerators (IP Address for them)\n\n\no       -I noticed on the last Epi
 c status report that there is going to be a new OnBase scanner that is bein
 g used at PHN to be installed at 1340 in the next month or so.  This is the
  new OCR replacement for  Epic Tapestry.  Please ensure that we have a spot
  for it in the drawings at 1450 OPC.  (from Cindy)\n\no       -Question: wh
 o is responsible for knowing what applications should be installed on the P
 C and how it’s used? (the ITS Coord/Mgr or the Department Mgr or Someone fr
 om Epic)\n\no       -SR for Raf.\,  PC  with 2 monitors and Software Adobe 
 Pro.  (there is an existing PC name: TKNOW0145 that Raf. L. is using now)\n
